ounced the Intel grand  slam which is a competition featuring a  1 million dollar prize pool for the  first team to win 4 of the 10 major  counter strike go competition to be  clear this is a bonus prize on top of  the prize that these teams are already  going to win  pretty amazing they also announced the  VR challenger league and eSports  competition that will focus on virtual  reality it will feature insomniac the  unspoken and echo arena a VR multiplayer  game from ready at dawn which by the way  will be free for all oculus rift owners  when it releases on July 20th look for  the single-player campaign lone echo on  the same release date the VR Challenger  League will culminate in 2018 with a  championship at the Intel Extreme  Masters in Poland fire axis announced a  MIDI XCOM 2 expansion called war of the  chosen it promises new environments new  enemies and new XCOM forces three  champions will be featured who will grow  and strength throughout the game as they  learn new skills and abilities there are  also new zombie like hordes of creatures  called The Lost that will attack alien  and humans so look out plus there are  resistance groups to win over most  importantly fair access set it is easily  twice the size of the last expansion so  you're going to have lots to get your  hands on on August 29th there is no  denying player unknowns battlegrounds is  taking twitch by storm  creator Brendan Green took the stage to  announce some changes that are coming to  the game according to game spots Alex  Newhouse one of the most significant  additions the ability to vault over  objects this will likely make fans very  happy as current mechanics make it  extremely difficult to get over fences  rocks and other small obstacles as a  result it can be frustrating to navigate  through the map in addition the studio  is making new weather effects for the  game right now the map features only  clear skies or downpour but there will  soon be sunset and fog variants as well  